__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Caches are rebuildable from a config and a seed. Anchored to the repo root: a
# bare `data/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, and quietly
# excluded `symbolic_ai_models/data/` -- the harness itself -- from every commit
# this repo has ever made.
/data/

# Runs: keep the evidence, drop the weights.
#
# `README.md` and `RESEARCH_LOG.md` cite eight run directories as the source of
# every published number, and all of it was untracked -- so on a fresh clone the
# floors, the configs each row was measured under, and the numbers themselves
# were simply gone. For a repo whose rule is that a number without a floor is
# not a result, the floors have to survive a clone.
#
# `summary.json` carries the config, the floors and the metrics; `rules.txt` is
# the legible artifact a reader is invited to argue with. Together they are 332K
# against 732M of checkpoints, and they make the "did these rows share a config?"
# audit possible after the fact -- a check this repo has already been bitten by.
#
# `policy.txt` joined them on 2026-08-14, for the same reason and after the same
# kind of miss. It is the *only* place an agent's coverage is written down --
# "spoke on 2,620 of 2,703 decisions (96.9%)", the abstention rate, the
# shortcut's share of the prior -- and on `repair` a row is part mechanism and
# part coverage in a ratio nothing else records. A finding quoted "read straight
# off `policy.txt`" from a directory whose `policy.txt` had never been committed,
# so the one number that would have let a refuter separate the two was
# unavailable to them. It is a few hundred bytes per run.
#
# Directories must be re-included explicitly or git will not descend into them
# to find the negations.
#
# `copyable_split.txt` joined them on 2026-08-15, for the third instance of the
# same miss. `label_acc` is 72% a copy score, so the number a note argues about
# is usually `acc | not copyable` -- and that split is **not** in
# `summary.json`. It is produced by `scripts/copyable_split.py`, which needs the
# run's `model.pt`, which this file deliberately drops. So the split was
# recomputable only by re-running the whole sweep, and a finding that rests on
# it had no artefact a reader could check. A few hundred bytes per arm.
/runs/**
!/runs/**/
!/runs/**/summary.json
!/runs/**/rules.txt
!/runs/**/policy.txt
!/runs/**/copyable_split.txt

# Knowledge-graph ingestion: keep the manifest, drop the corpus.
#
# The same rule as `/runs/**` above, applied to a different kind of bulk. The
# source corpora are ~14 GB and every byte of them is re-fetchable from
# upstream; the mined and normalised intermediates are larger still and are a
# pure function of (source, miner, config). None of that belongs in a 27 MB
# repository, and a clone that dragged it would be unusable.
#
# What *must* survive a clone is the answer to "what produced this graph?" —
# which source files, at which checksums, through which miner, yielding how
# many facts, rejecting how many, under which schema version. That is what a
# `manifest.json` records, and it is the exact analogue of `summary.json`: the
# artefact that lets a later reader audit a number instead of taking it on
# trust. This repo's standing rule is that a number without its floor is not a
# result; a mined fact without its provenance is the same defect one layer down,
# and it is worse here because the two ingestion paths (parsed vs
# directly-mined) will not produce facts of equal quality. Pooling them without
# recording which path produced which is how `label_acc` spent its entire
# history hiding a 72:28 mixture.
#
# `schema.json` is tracked for the same reason: normalisation is a design
# decision, it will be revised, and a graph whose schema is not pinned cannot be
# compared against an earlier one.
#
# Small, licensed, sha-pinned *derived* graphs do not live here at all — they go
# in `symbolic_ai_kg/data/` and are tracked in full, as `wordnet30-physical`
# (248K) and `cskg-commonsense` (612K) already are. The rule of thumb: if a
# model reads it at sweep time, vendor it; if it is scaffolding on the way to
# producing that, it belongs under `/kg/` and only its manifest survives.
#
# Directories must be re-included explicitly or git will not descend into them
# to find the negations.
/kg/**
!/kg/**/
!/kg/README.md
!/kg/**/manifest.json
!/kg/**/schema.json
!/kg/**/stats*.json
!/kg/**/LICENSE*
